Identify the historical context of the Year of the Four Emperors and the sequence of emperors during that period.
The historical context of the Year of the Four Emperors refers to the period in ancient Rome from 69 AD to 70 AD, during which four different emperors ruled the Roman Empire in quick succession. The sequence of emperors during this period was:

1.  Galba (June 68 - January 69 AD)
2.  Otho (January - April 69 AD)
3.  Vitellius (April - December 69 AD)
4.  Vespasian (December 69 - 79 AD)

This period was marked by civil war, power struggles, and instability, ultimately leading to the end of the Julio-Claudian dynasty and the beginning of the Flavian dynasty.
